{"availability":"available","full":"Sammysystems/realestate-portal","name":"realestate-portal","description":"Ops desk for real-estate agencies - the gaps that lose deals, closed. Every lead on a 4h SLA clock, auto first-reply from real property facts, land-search stalls flagged with day limits, inspections and follow-ups on one screen, every email logged. React + Vercel + Postgres.","category":"Design","language":"TypeScript","stars":0,"forks":0,"created":"2026-10-08T14:56:16Z","updated":"2026-10-10T12:33:52Z","branch":"master","homepage":"https://realestate-portal-ten.vercel.app","topics":["dashboard","email-automation","lead-management","postgresql","react","real-estate","real-estate-crm","serverless","tailwindcss","typescript","vercel","vite"],"demo":"https://realestate-portal-ten.vercel.app/","color":"#323057","ink":"#d6caff","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-12T07:59:54.391Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-12T07:59:54.391Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-12T07:59:54.391Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-12T07:59:54.391Z","stars":0,"forks":0}],"technologies":["React"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Agencies don't lose deals in the office. They lose them in the gaps: a lead waiting nine hours for a first reply, a land search stalled eighteen days before anyone notices, a follow-up remembered on Friday for a Tuesday inquiry. Nobody can say who was emailed what, or when.","This system closes those gaps. One screen where every lead carries a clock, every stall is flagged the day it happens, and the reply goes out before the buyer moves on to the next listing. And it's not just a board — an assistant answers questions about the book and drafts the chase.","Live demo: (login: any token set as REPADMINTOKEN — seed data included)"],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/Sammysystems/realestate-portal/blob/master/README.md","fingerprint":"0e9ca8ed8799c0262bb72a3fd04a394fcc8753198577bd7516fd67ee3237dd84","extractedAt":"2026-10-12T07:59:54.625Z"},"overviewCheckedAt"